<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p>Last updated: 8 November 2026</p>
<h2>1. Introduction</h2>
<p>This policy explains how LinkSnap handles information when you use the application.</p>
<h2>2. Information you provide</h2>
<p>Information entered to generate QR codes is processed by the app to create those codes. The app also stores saved QR history, collections and preferences locally on your device.</p>
<h2>3. Photos</h2>
<p>When you choose a photo for Photo Studio, it is used to customise your QR code. The app does not operate its own photo-upload service.</p>
<h2>4. Advertising</h2>
<p>LinkSnap uses Google AdMob to display advertisements. Google and its advertising partners may collect device and usage information to provide and measure ads, subject to their applicable policies and settings.</p>
<p>Learn more: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
<h2>5. Data sharing</h2>
<p>LinkSnap does not operate its own user-account or cloud-storage service. Information handled by third-party services, including advertising providers, is subject to their own privacy policies.</p>
<h2>6. Data control</h2>
<p>You can manage saved QR codes and app preferences within the app. Uninstalling the app may remove locally stored app data.</p>
<h2>7. Children</h2>
<p>LinkSnap is not designed to knowingly collect personal information directly from children.</p>
<h2>8. Changes</h2>
<p>This policy may be updated as the app changes. The latest version will be published on this page.</p>
